From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow DT firmware directory override

QCN9224 uses PCI ID 0x1109, which upstream maps to the QCN9274
hardware parameters and consequently to QCN9274/hw2.0.  Boards such as
the TP-Link BE65 V2 instead ship compatible firmware and board data in
QCN92XX/hw1.0.

Add a qcom,firmware-directory property which replaces the hardware
parameter directory for every firmware request, including board and
regulatory data.  Keep the existing firmware-name use-case subdirectory
semantics when the new property is absent.

This is deliberately opt-in so genuine QCN9274 devices sharing the PCI
ID keep their upstream firmware directory.

Signed-off-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
index 829ad4f..3b2afb6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -1360,8 +1360,16 @@ static inline void ath12k_core_create_firmware_path(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 						    const char *filename,
 						    void *buf, size_t buf_len)
 {
+	const char *fw_dir = NULL;
 	const char *fw_name = NULL;
 
+	if (!of_property_read_string(ab->dev->of_node,
+				     "qcom,firmware-directory", &fw_dir)) {
+		snprintf(buf, buf_len, "%s/%s/%s", ATH12K_FW_DIR,
+			 fw_dir, filename);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (ab->hif.bus == ATH12K_BUS_PCI)
 		of_property_read_string(ab->dev->of_node, "firmware-name", &fw_name);
 
